IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 23 to 27: appointments under powers, the executor as trustee, the chain of executors, the devisee and
-- mortgage debts, and the estate that accrues to the Government (bona vacantia).
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".
-- Section 27(3) to (5) give powers to the Minister; they are encoded here as Layer 1 functions but the seat takes no question on them.

§ `Section 23 -- appointments valid notwithstanding exclusion of objects or an unsubstantial share`

-- src:1480 | 23.—(1) Where by any deed, will or other instrument a power is
-- src:1481 | given to appoint movable or immovable property amongst several
-- src:1482 | objects in such manner that no one of the objects of the power can be
-- src:1483 | excluded, or some one or more of the objects of the power cannot be
-- src:1484 | excluded by the donee of the power from a share of that property, but
-- src:1485 | without requiring a substantial share of that property to be given to
-- src:1486 | each object of the power or to each object of the power who cannot be
-- src:1491 | excluded, no appointment, which has been or is after 23 July 1909
-- src:1492 | made in exercise of any such power or authority, shall be invalid on
-- src:1493 | the ground that an unsubstantial, illusory or nominal share only is
-- src:1494 | thereby appointed, or left unappointed to devolve upon any one or
-- src:1495 | more of the objects of the power or on the ground that any object of
-- src:1496 | that power has been altogether excluded.
@ref s 23(1) (src:1480-1496)
GIVEN `the power is given by a deed will or other instrument to appoint property amongst several objects so that no one or more of them can be excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument does not require a substantial share to be given to each object or to each object who cannot be excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground asserted is that an unsubstantial illusory or nominal share only is appointed or left unappointed or that an object has been altogether excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) the appointment is invalid on the ground asserted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the power is given by a deed will or other instrument to appoint property amongst several objects so that no one or more of them can be excluded` AND `the instrument does not require a substantial share to be given to each object or to each object who cannot be excluded`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where by any deed, will or other instrument a power is given to appoint ... in such manner that no one of the objects of the power can be excluded ... but without requiring a substantial share of that property to be given to each object" -- fork F-23: "which has been or is after 23 July 1909 made" is read as reaching every appointment, so no date gate
        IF `the ground asserted is that an unsubstantial illusory or nominal share only is appointed or left unappointed or that an object has been altogether excluded` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no appointment ... shall be invalid on the ground that an unsubstantial, illusory or nominal share only is thereby appointed, or left unappointed to devolve upon any one or more of the objects of the power or on the ground that any object of that power has been altogether excluded"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that"; an appointment invalid on another ground is not addressed

-- src:1498 | (2) Every such appointment shall be valid and effectual
-- src:1499 | notwithstanding that any one or more of the objects does or do not
-- src:1500 | thereunder, or in default thereof, take more than an unsubstantial,
-- src:1501 | illusory or nominal share, and notwithstanding that any one or more
-- src:1502 | of the objects does or do not thereunder, or in default thereof, take a
-- src:1503 | share or shares of the said property.
@ref s 23(2) (src:1498-1503)
GIVEN `the appointment is an appointment within subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) the appointment is valid and effectual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointment is an appointment within subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every such appointment"

-- src:1507 | (3) Nothing in this section shall prejudice or affect any provision in
-- src:1508 | any deed, will or other instrument creating any such power as
-- src:1509 | aforesaid, which declares the amount of the share or shares from
-- src:1510 | which no object of the power shall be excluded.
@ref s 23(3) (src:1507-1510)
GIVEN `the provision is in the instrument creating the power and declares the amount of the share or shares from which no object of the power shall be excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(3) section 23 prejudices or affects the provision declaring the amount of the share` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision is in the instrument creating the power and declares the amount of the share or shares from which no object of the power shall be excluded` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall prejudice or affect any provision in any deed, will or other instrument creating any such power as aforesaid, which declares the amount of the share or shares from which no object of the power shall be excluded"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision in any deed, will or other instrument creating any such power as aforesaid, which declares the amount of the share"

-- src:1515 | (4) Nothing in this section shall be construed, deemed or taken to
-- src:1516 | give any other validity, force or effect to any appointment than such
-- src:1517 | appointment would have had if a substantial share of the property
-- src:1518 | affected by the power had been thereby appointed, or left
-- src:1519 | unappointed.
@ref s 23(4) (src:1515-1519)
GIVEN `the validity force or effect claimed for the appointment is other than it would have had if a substantial share of the property had been appointed or left unappointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(4) section 23 gives the appointment the validity force or effect claimed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the validity force or effect claimed for the appointment is other than it would have had if a substantial share of the property had been appointed or left unappointed` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall be construed, deemed or taken to give any other validity, force or effect to any appointment than such appointment would have had if a substantial share of the property affected by the power had been thereby appointed, or left unappointed"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other validity, force or effect"

§ `Section 24 -- executor deemed to be trustee for the person entitled to residue on intestacy`

-- src:1524 | 24. When any person dies or has died, having by his will appointed
-- src:1525 | any person to be his executor, such executor shall be deemed to be a
-- src:1526 | trustee for the person, if any, who would be entitled to the estate in
-- src:1527 | case the person died intestate in respect of any residue not expressly
-- src:1528 | disposed of, unless it appears by the will that the person so appointed
-- src:1529 | executor was intended to take such residue beneficially.
@ref s 24 (src:1524-1529)
GIVEN `the person has by his will appointed a person to be his executor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is residue not expressly disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears by the will that the person appointed executor was intended to take the residue beneficially` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24 the executor is deemed to be a trustee for the person entitled in case of intestacy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person has by his will appointed a person to be his executor` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When any person dies or has died, having by his will appointed any person to be his executor, such executor shall be deemed to be a trustee" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "when" is read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling)
        IF NOT `the property is residue not expressly disposed of` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any residue not expressly disposed of"
        IF `it appears by the will that the person appointed executor was intended to take the residue beneficially` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it appears by the will that the person so appointed executor was intended to take such residue beneficially" -- an exception to a deeming: the deeming does not apply
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 25 -- executor of executor represents original testator`

-- src:1536 | 25.—(1) An executor of a sole or last surviving executor of a
-- src:1537 | testator is the executor of that testator.
@ref s 25(1) (src:1536-1537)
GIVEN `the person is an executor of a sole or last surviving executor of a testator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) the person is the executor of that testator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an executor of a sole or last surviving executor of a testator` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An executor of a sole or last surviving executor of a testator"

-- src:1539 | (2) Subsection (1) shall not apply to an executor who does not prove
-- src:1540 | the will of his testator and, in the case of an executor who on his death
-- src:1541 | leaves surviving him some other executor of his testator who
-- src:1542 | afterwards proves the will of that testator, it shall cease to apply on
-- src:1543 | such probate being granted.
@ref s 25(2) (src:1539-1543)
GIVEN `the executor proves the will of his testator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on his death he leaves surviving him another executor of his testator who afterwards proves the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the executor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the executor proves the will of his testator` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) shall not apply to an executor who does not prove the will of his testator"
        IF `on his death he leaves surviving him another executor of his testator who afterwards proves the will` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an executor who on his death leaves surviving him some other executor of his testator who afterwards proves the will of that testator, it shall cease to apply on such probate being granted"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection takes two cases out and says nothing of any other

-- Hand-gathering function (ruling E1, option B as guidance): the executor of the executor, reading (2) before (1).
-- src:1536 | 25.—(1) An executor of a sole or last surviving executor of a
-- src:1537 | testator is the executor of that testator.
-- src:1539 | (2) Subsection (1) shall not apply to an executor who does not prove
-- src:1540 | the will of his testator and, in the case of an executor who on his death
-- src:1541 | leaves surviving him some other executor of his testator who
-- src:1542 | afterwards proves the will of that testator, it shall cease to apply on
-- src:1543 | such probate being granted.
@ref s 25(1) and (2) gathered (src:1536-1543)
GIVEN `the person is an executor of a sole or last surviving executor of a testator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the executor proves the will of his testator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on his death he leaves surviving him another executor of his testator who afterwards proves the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) with (2) the person is the executor of that testator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the executor` `the executor proves the will of his testator` `on his death he leaves surviving him another executor of his testator who afterwards proves the will`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) shall not apply" (s 25(2))
    OTHERWISE `s 25(1) the person is the executor of that testator` `the person is an executor of a sole or last surviving executor of a testator`

-- src:1545 | (3) So long as the chain of such representation is unbroken, the last
-- src:1546 | executor in the chain is the executor of every preceding testator.
@ref s 25(3) (src:1545-1546)
GIVEN `the chain of such representation is unbroken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(3) the last executor in the chain is the executor of every preceding testator` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the chain of such representation is unbroken` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "So long as the chain of such representation is unbroken, the last executor in the chain is the executor of every preceding testator"

-- src:1548 | (4) The chain of such representation is broken by —
-- src:1550 | (a) an intestacy;
-- src:1552 | (b) the failure of a testator to appoint an executor; or
-- src:1554 | (c) the failure to obtain a probate of a will,
-- src:1556 | but is not broken by a temporary grant of administration if probate is
-- src:1557 | subsequently granted.
@ref s 25(4) (src:1548-1557)
GIVEN `there is an intestacy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a testator fails to appoint an executor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a failure to obtain a probate of a will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant is a temporary grant of administration and probate is subsequently granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(4) the chain of such representation is broken` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the grant is a temporary grant of administration and probate is subsequently granted` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but is not broken by a temporary grant of administration if probate is subsequently granted"
        IF `there is an intestacy` OR `a testator fails to appoint an executor` OR `there is a failure to obtain a probate of a will` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names three breaks and one non-break and does not say that no other event breaks the chain

-- src:1559 | (5) Every person in the chain of representation to a testator —
-- src:1561 | (a) has the same rights in respect of the estate of that testator as
-- src:1562 | the original executor would have had if living; and
@ref s 25(5)(a) (src:1559-1562)
GIVEN `the person is in the chain of representation to a testator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(5)(a) the person has the same rights in respect of the estate as the original executor would have had if living` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is in the chain of representation to a testator` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person in the chain of representation to a testator"

-- src:1559 | (5) Every person in the chain of representation to a testator —
-- src:1564 | (b) is, to the extent to which the estate of that testator has come
-- src:1565 | to his hands, answerable as if he were an original executor.
@ref s 25(5)(b) (src:1559-1565)
GIVEN `the person is in the chain of representation to a testator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estate of that testator has come to his hands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(5)(b) the person is answerable as if he were an original executor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is in the chain of representation to a testator` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person in the chain of representation to a testator"
        IF `the estate of that testator has come to his hands` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent to which the estate of that testator has come to his hands"

§ `Section 26 -- devisee of land not to claim payment of mortgage debt out of movable property`

-- src:1570 | 26.—(1) If any person dies or has died seised of or entitled to any
-- src:1571 | estate or interest in any immovable property, which is at the time of
-- src:1572 | his death charged with the payment of any sum or sums of money by
-- src:1573 | way of mortgage, and such person has not by his will or deed or other
-- src:1574 | document signified any contrary or other intention, the devisee to
-- src:1575 | whom such immovable property is devised shall not be entitled to
-- src:1576 | have the mortgage debt discharged or satisfied out of the movable
-- src:1577 | property or any other immovable property of that person.
@ref s 26(1) (src:1570-1577)
GIVEN `the person dies or has died seised of or entitled to an estate or interest in immovable property which is at the time of his death charged by way of mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is the devisee to whom the immovable property is devised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has by his will or deed or other document signified a contrary or other intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the devisee is entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged out of the movable property or any other immovable property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person dies or has died seised of or entitled to an estate or interest in immovable property which is at the time of his death charged by way of mortgage` AND `the claimant is the devisee to whom the immovable property is devised`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person dies or has died seised of or entitled to any estate or interest in any immovable property, which is at the time of his death charged ... the devisee to whom such immovable property is devised"
        IF `the person has by his will or deed or other document signified a contrary or other intention` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and such person has not by his will or deed or other document signified any contrary or other intention" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the devisee to whom such immovable property is devised shall not be entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged or satisfied out of the movable property or any other immovable property of that person"

-- src:1582 | (2) The immovable property so charged shall as between the
-- src:1583 | different persons claiming through or under the deceased person be
-- src:1584 | primarily liable to the payment of all mortgage debts with which the
-- src:1585 | same is charged, every part thereof according to its value bearing a
-- src:1586 | proportionate part of the mortgage debts charged on the whole
-- src:1587 | thereof.
@ref s 26(2) (src:1582-1587)
GIVEN `the persons claim through or under the deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is immovable property charged with mortgage debts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) the immovable property is primarily liable to the payment of the mortgage debts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the persons claim through or under the deceased person` AND `the property is immovable property charged with mortgage debts` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as between the different persons claiming through or under the deceased person" and "the immovable property so charged"

-- src:1585 | same is charged, every part thereof according to its value bearing a
-- src:1586 | proportionate part of the mortgage debts charged on the whole
-- src:1587 | thereof.
@ref s 26(2) the proportionate part (src:1585-1587)
GIVEN `the persons claim through or under the deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is immovable property charged with mortgage debts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the part` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the whole` IS A NUMBER
      `the mortgage debts charged on the whole` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 26(2) the part of the immovable property bears this share of the mortgage debts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 26(2) the immovable property is primarily liable to the payment of the mortgage debts` `the persons claim through or under the deceased person` `the property is immovable property charged with mortgage debts` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the value of the whole` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST ((`the mortgage debts charged on the whole` TIMES `the value of the part`) / `the value of the whole`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every part thereof according to its value bearing a proportionate part of the mortgage debts charged on the whole thereof"

-- src:1589 | (3) In the construction of the will of any person, a general direction
-- src:1590 | that the debts of the testator shall be paid out of his personal estate
-- src:1591 | shall not be deemed to be a declaration of an intention contrary to or
-- src:1592 | other than the rule contained in this section unless such contrary or
-- src:1593 | other intention is further declared by words expressly or by necessary
-- src:1594 | implication referring to all or some of the testator’s debts or debt
-- src:1595 | charged by way of mortgage on any part of his immovable estate.
@ref s 26(3) (src:1589-1595)
GIVEN `the direction is a general direction that the debts of the testator shall be paid out of his personal estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary or other intention is further declared by words expressly or by necessary implication referring to all or some of the testator's debts or debt charged by way of mortgage on any part of his immovable estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(3) the general direction is deemed to be a declaration of an intention contrary to the rule in this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the direction is a general direction that the debts of the testator shall be paid out of his personal estate` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a general direction that the debts of the testator shall be paid out of his personal estate"
        IF `a contrary or other intention is further declared by words expressly or by necessary implication referring to all or some of the testator's debts or debt charged by way of mortgage on any part of his immovable estate` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless such contrary or other intention is further declared" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be deemed to be a declaration of an intention contrary to or other than the rule contained in this section"

-- src:1597 | (4) In this section, “mortgage” shall be deemed to extend to any lien
-- src:1598 | for unpaid purchase‑money upon any immovable property purchased
-- src:1599 | by a testator.
@ref s 26(4) (src:1597-1599)
GIVEN `it is a lien for unpaid purchase-money upon immovable property purchased by a testator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(4) the lien is a mortgage for the purposes of section 26` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a lien for unpaid purchase-money upon immovable property purchased by a testator` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“mortgage” shall be deemed to extend to any lien for unpaid purchase-money"

-- src:1601 | (5) Nothing in this section shall affect or diminish any right of the
-- src:1602 | mortgagee of such immovable property to obtain full payment or
-- src:1603 | satisfaction of his mortgage debt, either out of the estate of the person
-- src:1604 | so dying as aforesaid or otherwise.
@ref s 26(5) (src:1601-1604)
GIVEN `the right is a right of the mortgagee of the immovable property to obtain full payment or satisfaction of his mortgage debt out of the estate of the person so dying or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(5) section 26 affects or diminishes the right of the mortgagee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the right is a right of the mortgagee of the immovable property to obtain full payment or satisfaction of his mortgage debt out of the estate of the person so dying or otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall affect or diminish any right of the mortgagee of such immovable property to obtain full payment or satisfaction of his mortgage debt"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any right of the mortgagee of such immovable property"

§ `Section 27 -- bona vacantia`

-- src:1608 | 27.—(1) This section applies —
-- src:1610 | (a) where a right to the estate of any person who dies (whether
-- src:1611 | before, on or after 15 February 2013) intestate without
-- src:1612 | next‑of‑kin has accrued to the Government; or
-- src:1614 | (b) where a right to the property of any person who dies
-- src:1615 | (whether before, on or after 15 February 2013) has accrued
-- src:1616 | to the Government as a result of disposal under such
-- src:1617 | written law as the Minister may, by order published in the
-- src:1618 | Gazette, prescribe for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 27(1) (src:1608-1618)
GIVEN `a right to the estate of a person who dies intestate without next-of-kin has accrued to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a right to the property of a person who dies has accrued to the Government as a result of disposal under a written law that the Minister has prescribed by order published in the Gazette for the purposes of this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) section 27 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a right to the estate of a person who dies intestate without next-of-kin has accrued to the Government` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `a right to the property of a person who dies has accrued to the Government as a result of disposal under a written law that the Minister has prescribed by order published in the Gazette for the purposes of this section`
            WHEN JUST x THEN
                IF x THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies — (a) where a right to the estate of any person who dies ... intestate without next-of-kin has accrued to the Government; or (b) where a right to the property of any person who dies ... has accrued to the Government as a result of disposal under such written law as the Minister may ... prescribe" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such written law as the Minister may, by order published in the Gazette, prescribe" -- no order is among the sources

-- src:1622 | (2) Where a right to any estate or property upon the death of a
-- src:1623 | person as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued to the
-- src:1624 | Government, such estate, property or part thereof that is not land,
-- src:1629 | or where such estate or property or part thereof is land and that land is
-- src:1630 | sold, its proceeds, shall form part of the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 27(2) (src:1622-1630)
GIVEN `section 27 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land has been sold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the estate or property or the proceeds of the land form part of the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `section 27 applies` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a right to any estate or property upon the death of a person as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued to the Government, such estate, property or part thereof ... shall form part of the Consolidated Fund" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no
        IF NOT `the thing is land` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the land has been sold` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where such estate or property or part thereof is land and that land is sold, its proceeds" -- unsold land is not addressed

-- src:1634 | (3) If it appears to the Minister that a right to any estate or property
-- src:1635 | upon the death of a person as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued
-- src:1636 | to the Government, it shall be lawful for the Minister, upon
-- src:1637 | application being made to him or if he considers it reasonable to
-- src:1638 | do so, by warrant under his hand —
-- src:1640 | (a) to disclaim and release in whole or in part that right to such
-- src:1641 | estate or property in favour of such person or persons who
-- src:1642 | establish to the satisfaction of the Minister any equitable or
-- src:1643 | moral claim thereto; and
@ref s 27(3)(a) (src:1634-1643)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister that a right to estate or property upon a death as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `application is made to the Minister or he considers it reasonable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes to the satisfaction of the Minister an equitable or moral claim to the estate or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(3)(a) the Minister may by warrant disclaim and release the right in favour of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it appears to the Minister that a right to estate or property upon a death as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued to the Government` AND `application is made to the Minister or he considers it reasonable to do so`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it appears to the Minister that a right ... has accrued to the Government, it shall be lawful for the Minister, upon application being made to him or if he considers it reasonable to do so, by warrant under his hand" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" or "upon" is the text's no
        IF `the person establishes to the satisfaction of the Minister an equitable or moral claim to the estate or property` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in favour of such person or persons who establish to the satisfaction of the Minister any equitable or moral claim thereto"

-- src:1634 | (3) If it appears to the Minister that a right to any estate or property
-- src:1635 | upon the death of a person as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued
-- src:1636 | to the Government, it shall be lawful for the Minister, upon
-- src:1637 | application being made to him or if he considers it reasonable to
-- src:1638 | do so, by warrant under his hand —
-- src:1645 | (b) to authorise or order the giving, conveyance, transfer, grant
-- src:1646 | or payment, out of the whole or any part of such estate or
-- src:1647 | property or (if sold) its proceeds, in such share, proportion
-- src:1648 | and manner and upon such terms and conditions as the
-- src:1649 | Minister thinks appropriate (whether or not including the
-- src:1650 | payment of moneys) to that person or those persons, as the
-- src:1651 | case may be.
@ref s 27(3)(b) (src:1634-1651)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister that a right to estate or property upon a death as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `application is made to the Minister or he considers it reasonable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes to the satisfaction of the Minister an equitable or moral claim to the estate or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(3)(b) the Minister may by warrant authorise or order the giving or payment out of the estate or property to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it appears to the Minister that a right to estate or property upon a death as mentioned in subsection (1) has accrued to the Government` AND `application is made to the Minister or he considers it reasonable to do so`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it appears to the Minister that a right ... has accrued to the Government, it shall be lawful for the Minister, upon application being made to him or if he considers it reasonable to do so" -- MARGINAL (a)
        IF `the person establishes to the satisfaction of the Minister an equitable or moral claim to the estate or property` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to that person or those persons, as the case may be"

-- src:1655 | (4) Upon a right of the Government being disclaimed and released
-- src:1656 | by warrant under subsection (3), the following provisions shall apply:
-- src:1658 | (a) any moneys specified in any such warrant shall, if forming
-- src:1659 | part of the Consolidated Fund, be charged on and paid out
-- src:1660 | of the Consolidated Fund without further authority other
-- src:1661 | than this section;
@ref s 27(4)(a) (src:1655-1661)
GIVEN `the right of the Government has been disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moneys are specified in the warrant and form part of the Consolidated Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(4)(a) the moneys specified in the warrant are charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund without further authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the right of the Government has been disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon a right of the Government being disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3), the following provisions shall apply" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "upon" is read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling)
        IF `the moneys are specified in the warrant and form part of the Consolidated Fund` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any moneys specified in any such warrant shall, if forming part of the Consolidated Fund"

-- src:1655 | (4) Upon a right of the Government being disclaimed and released
-- src:1656 | by warrant under subsection (3), the following provisions shall apply:
-- src:1663 | (b) any other movable property specified in the warrant that is
-- src:1664 | the subject of the disclaimer and release shall vest, by
-- src:1665 | virtue of that warrant and without any conveyance,
-- src:1666 | assignment or further assurance, in the person or persons
-- src:1667 | in favour of whom the disclaimer and release is made in
-- src:1668 | such share, proportion and manner as are specified in the
-- src:1669 | warrant; and
@ref s 27(4)(b) (src:1655-1669)
GIVEN `the right of the Government has been disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is other movable property specified in the warrant that is the subject of the disclaimer and release` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(4)(b) the movable property vests in the person without conveyance assignment or further assurance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the right of the Government has been disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon a right of the Government being disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3), the following provisions shall apply" -- MARGINAL (a)
        IF `the property is other movable property specified in the warrant that is the subject of the disclaimer and release` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other movable property specified in the warrant that is the subject of the disclaimer and release"

-- src:1655 | (4) Upon a right of the Government being disclaimed and released
-- src:1656 | by warrant under subsection (3), the following provisions shall apply:
-- src:1671 | (c) any warrant ordering the grant or lease of any State land or
-- src:1672 | interest therein shall have the effect of authorising a grant
-- src:1673 | or lease of the land under the State Lands Act 1920 to the
-- src:1678 | person or persons in favour of whom the disclaimer and
-- src:1679 | release is made in such share, proportion and manner as are
-- src:1680 | specified in the warrant.
@ref s 27(4)(c) (src:1655-1680)
GIVEN `the right of the Government has been disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant orders the grant or lease of State land or an interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(4)(c) the warrant has the effect of authorising a grant or lease under the State Lands Act 1920` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the right of the Government has been disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon a right of the Government being disclaimed and released by warrant under subsection (3), the following provisions shall apply" -- MARGINAL (a)
        IF `the warrant orders the grant or lease of State land or an interest in it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any warrant ordering the grant or lease of any State land or interest therein"

-- src:1684 | (5) For the avoidance of doubt, a disclaimer and release by warrant
-- src:1685 | under subsection (3) may be made without actual entry into or taking
-- src:1686 | of possession of the estate or property in question being first made by
-- src:1687 | the Government.
@ref s 27(5) (src:1684-1687)
GIVEN `the disclaimer and release is by warrant under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(5) actual entry into or taking of possession by the Government must first be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclaimer and release is by warrant under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a disclaimer and release by warrant under subsection (3) may be made without actual entry into or taking of possession of the estate or property in question being first made by the Government"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a disclaimer and release by warrant under subsection (3)"

-- src:1691 | (6) Nothing in this section shall affect the disposal of any property
-- src:1692 | according to Muslim law.
@ref s 27(6) (src:1691-1692)
GIVEN `the property is disposed of according to Muslim law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(6) section 27 affects the disposal of the property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the property is disposed of according to Muslim law` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall affect the disposal of any property according to Muslim law"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the disposal of any property according to Muslim law"

§§ `Sections 23 to 27 -- tests`

-- s 23
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the appointment is invalid on the ground asserted` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall be invalid on the ground that an unsubstantial, illusory or nominal share only is thereby appointed"
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the appointment is invalid on the ground asserted` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- invalid on another ground: not addressed
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the appointment is invalid on the ground asserted` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the instrument requires a substantial share: outside the section
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the appointment is invalid on the ground asserted` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a power of that kind
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the appointment is valid and effectual` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be valid and effectual"
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the appointment is valid and effectual` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not such an appointment
#ASSERT `s 23(3) section 23 prejudices or affects the provision declaring the amount of the share` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Nothing in this section shall prejudice or affect"
#ASSERT `s 23(3) section 23 prejudices or affects the provision declaring the amount of the share` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another provision
#ASSERT `s 23(4) section 23 gives the appointment the validity force or effect claimed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Nothing in this section shall be construed ... to give any other validity, force or effect"
#ASSERT `s 23(4) section 23 gives the appointment the validity force or effect claimed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the effect claimed is no other
-- s 24
#ASSERT `s 24 the executor is deemed to be a trustee for the person entitled in case of intestacy` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be deemed to be a trustee"
#ASSERT `s 24 the executor is deemed to be a trustee for the person entitled in case of intestacy` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless it appears by the will that [he] was intended to take such residue beneficially"
#ASSERT `s 24 the executor is deemed to be a trustee for the person entitled in case of intestacy` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- property that is not undisposed residue
#ASSERT `s 24 the executor is deemed to be a trustee for the person entitled in case of intestacy` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no executor appointed by the will: "When"
-- s 25
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the person is the executor of that testator` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "is the executor of that testator"
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the person is the executor of that testator` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an executor of a sole or last surviving executor
#ASSERT `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the executor` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "does not prove the will of his testator"
#ASSERT `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the executor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- another executor survives and afterwards proves: "it shall cease to apply"
#ASSERT `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the executor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the subsection says nothing of this case
#ASSERT `s 25(1) with (2) the person is the executor of that testator` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- gathered: proves the will and no other executor proves
#ASSERT `s 25(1) with (2) the person is the executor of that testator` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- gathered: does not prove the will
#ASSERT `s 25(1) with (2) the person is the executor of that testator` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- gathered: not an executor of a sole or last surviving executor
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the last executor in the chain is the executor of every preceding testator` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "So long as the chain ... is unbroken"
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the last executor in the chain is the executor of every preceding testator` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the chain is broken
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the chain of such representation is broken` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) an intestacy
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the chain of such representation is broken` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) failure to appoint an executor
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the chain of such representation is broken` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c) failure to obtain probate
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the chain of such representation is broken` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "not broken by a temporary grant of administration if probate is subsequently granted"
#ASSERT `s 25(4) the chain of such representation is broken` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- some other event: the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 25(5)(a) the person has the same rights in respect of the estate as the original executor would have had if living` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "has the same rights"
#ASSERT `s 25(5)(a) the person has the same rights in respect of the estate as the original executor would have had if living` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not in the chain
#ASSERT `s 25(5)(b) the person is answerable as if he were an original executor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- to the extent the estate has come to his hands
#ASSERT `s 25(5)(b) the person is answerable as if he were an original executor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "to the extent": none has come to his hands
#ASSERT `s 25(5)(b) the person is answerable as if he were an original executor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not in the chain
-- s 26
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the devisee is entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged out of the movable property or any other immovable property` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not be entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged"
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the devisee is entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged out of the movable property or any other immovable property` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a contrary intention was signified: a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the devisee is entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged out of the movable property or any other immovable property` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not immovable property charged by mortgage at death
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the devisee is entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged out of the movable property or any other immovable property` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not the devisee
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the immovable property is primarily liable to the payment of the mortgage debts` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "primarily liable"
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the immovable property is primarily liable to the payment of the mortgage debts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not as between persons claiming through the deceased
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the part of the immovable property bears this share of the mortgage debts` TRUE TRUE 100000 400000 200000 EQUALS JUST 50000 -- a quarter by value bears a quarter of the debts
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the part of the immovable property bears this share of the mortgage debts` FALSE TRUE 100000 400000 200000 EQUALS NOTHING -- not as between persons claiming through the deceased
#ASSERT `s 26(3) the general direction is deemed to be a declaration of an intention contrary to the rule in this section` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not be deemed to be a declaration"
#ASSERT `s 26(3) the general direction is deemed to be a declaration of an intention contrary to the rule in this section` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "unless" a contrary intention is further declared
#ASSERT `s 26(3) the general direction is deemed to be a declaration of an intention contrary to the rule in this section` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a general direction
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the lien is a mortgage for the purposes of section 26` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be deemed to extend to any lien for unpaid purchase-money"
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the lien is a mortgage for the purposes of section 26` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "extend" does not close the list
#ASSERT `s 26(5) section 26 affects or diminishes the right of the mortgagee` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Nothing in this section shall affect or diminish"
#ASSERT `s 26(5) section 26 affects or diminishes the right of the mortgagee` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another right
-- s 27
#ASSERT `s 27(1) section 27 applies` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) intestate without next-of-kin
#ASSERT `s 27(1) section 27 applies` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) a prescribed written law
#ASSERT `s 27(1) section 27 applies` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither: "where"
#ASSERT `s 27(1) section 27 applies` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- whether the Minister has prescribed a written law is not among the sources
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the estate or property or the proceeds of the land form part of the Consolidated Fund` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- property that is not land
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the estate or property or the proceeds of the land form part of the Consolidated Fund` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- land that is sold: its proceeds
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the estate or property or the proceeds of the land form part of the Consolidated Fund` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- land not sold
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the estate or property or the proceeds of the land form part of the Consolidated Fund` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- section 27 does not apply: "Where"
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(a) the Minister may by warrant disclaim and release the right in favour of the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "it shall be lawful for the Minister"
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(a) the Minister may by warrant disclaim and release the right in favour of the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no claim established to the Minister's satisfaction
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(a) the Minister may by warrant disclaim and release the right in favour of the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- it does not appear that a right accrued: "If"
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(a) the Minister may by warrant disclaim and release the right in favour of the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no application and not reasonable: "upon application ... or if he considers it reasonable"
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(b) the Minister may by warrant authorise or order the giving or payment out of the estate or property to the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "to authorise or order the giving, conveyance, transfer, grant or payment"
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(b) the Minister may by warrant authorise or order the giving or payment out of the estate or property to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not that person
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(b) the Minister may by warrant authorise or order the giving or payment out of the estate or property to the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "If it appears to the Minister"
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(a) the moneys specified in the warrant are charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund without further authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund"
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(a) the moneys specified in the warrant are charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund without further authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- moneys not specified in the warrant or not part of the Fund
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(a) the moneys specified in the warrant are charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund without further authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no warrant release: "Upon"
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(b) the movable property vests in the person without conveyance assignment or further assurance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall vest, by virtue of that warrant and without any conveyance"
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(b) the movable property vests in the person without conveyance assignment or further assurance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- property not specified in the warrant
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(b) the movable property vests in the person without conveyance assignment or further assurance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no warrant release
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(c) the warrant has the effect of authorising a grant or lease under the State Lands Act 1920` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall have the effect of authorising a grant or lease"
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(c) the warrant has the effect of authorising a grant or lease under the State Lands Act 1920` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a warrant not ordering a grant or lease of State land
#ASSERT `s 27(4)(c) the warrant has the effect of authorising a grant or lease under the State Lands Act 1920` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no warrant release
#ASSERT `s 27(5) actual entry into or taking of possession by the Government must first be made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "may be made without actual entry ... being first made"
#ASSERT `s 27(5) actual entry into or taking of possession by the Government must first be made` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another kind of disclaimer
#ASSERT `s 27(6) section 27 affects the disposal of the property` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "Nothing in this section shall affect the disposal of any property according to Muslim law"
#ASSERT `s 27(6) section 27 affects the disposal of the property` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another disposal
